# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the index and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a clone made with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the working
# tree while the index keeps LF, and the index caches the CRLF file size. Git then
# reports those files clean even though their bytes differ from the blob — until
# something touches one, at which point the whole file shows as modified. That
# silently broke SupportedBanksDocTest and BankSamplesDocTest here: both compare
# generated LF text against the checked-in file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep binaries byte-exact.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.zip binary
*.task binary
*.tflite binary
